GDN batch invariance under chunked prefill and prefix caching (onto v0.34.0
+ 0001).

The FLA prefill kernels split a sequence into 64-token chunks counted from
the first token of each prefill chunk. When the scheduler splits a prompt at
a position that is not a multiple of 64 (a chunk that shares the token
budget with other requests), or a prefill resumes from a prefix-cache hit off
that grid, the recurrent state is reduced in another order and the output
differs from the same prompt run alone. Measured on Imperial 2026-11-23: the
reviewer's test_logprobs_bitwise_batch_invariance_ragged_chunked_prefill fails
on every Qwen GDN model without this, and passes with the equivalent fix on
vllm main (the Privasys/vllm branch below). This port is not yet measured.

- Scheduler: with VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT and a GDN_ATTN Mamba group, every
  prefill chunk but the last ends on FLA_CHUNK_SIZE; a waiting prefill whose
  budget is below that waits a step.
- Platform: in align mode under VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT, the hybrid block size
  is a multiple of FLA_CHUNK_SIZE, so prefix-cache hits land on the grid.

Upstream form: Privasys/vllm gdn-batch-invariance (a layer-declared
prefill_chunk_alignment on main, where the Triton path already aligns blocks).

